      "status_as_recorded": "inconclusive",
      "finding": "Travel x fit quadrant predicts post-move minutes, usage, and net rating directionally (additive vs irrelevant embedded mpg 0.80 vs 0.68; dest net -0.63 vs -3.58), but correlations are weak (delta vs dest_net r=0.077) and risks of leakage and outcome-derived labels exist."
    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF32",
      "status_as_recorded": "artifact",
      "finding": "Rank-1 openers CUT-centered are infeasible in every team-game; CUT target 14-18% vs stretch ceiling 2-6%, indicating cut-heavy play-type mixes are severely constrained by personnel and system feasibility."
    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-APPA-052",
      "status_as_recorded": "supported",
      "finding": "Only 4 of 272 games exceeded CUT>15% of H2 mix; CUT-heavy games are extremely rare at the team level (base rate 1.5%)."
    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-088",
      "status_as_recorded": "supported",
      "finding": "Connector absence displaces team offensive identity (D_A=0.2020) more than usage-matched non-organizer absence (D_A=0.1021), demonstrating that certain structural roles (here connectors) have outsized influence and may behave differently in role travel."
