    {
      "code": "EXPOSURE_SPARSITY",
      "text": "CUT heavy profiles are infrequent; the share of shapers with CUT as a primary play type may be very small, undermining between-group comparisons or forcing arbitrary thresholds."
    },
    {
      "code": "MEASURE_RELIABILITY",
      "text": "CUT and DRIVE play types are subject to classification error; ambiguous possessions (e.g., drives off a cut) introduce noise into the independent variable."
    },
    {
      "code": "RTM_SELECTION",
      "text": "Players who change teams may differ systematically from those who stay; movers may be a selected set of shapers whose role was already misfitting, causing regression-to-the-mean artifacts in travel scores."
