    {
      "code": "CONFOUNDING",
      "text": "Role travel is confounded by age, injury history, destination team's scheme, and salary; without extensive controls, a raw comparison of cut-heavy vs drive-heavy travel scores is uninterpretable."
    },
    {
      "code": "DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY",
      "text": "Team offensive styles evolve; a shaper's pre-move play-type mix may reflect a system that no longer exists, making portability comparisons across seasons unreliable."
    },
    {
      "code": "MULTIPLE_TESTING",
      "text": "If multiple thresholds or multiple outcomes are explored, the risk of false positives inflates."
    }
  ],
  "predicted_outcome": {
    "supported": 0.05,
    "rejected": 0.05,
    "untestable": 0.55,
    "artifact": 0.15,
    "uncertain": 0.20
  },
  "decision": "do_not_proceed",
  "design": {
    "estimand": "Difference in mean travel score between cut-heavy shapers and drive-heavy shapers, where a shaper is defined as a player in the bottom 50% of team usage with positive residual structural influence, a cut-heavy shaper has CUT initiation share above the median among shapers and DRIVE share below median, and a drive-heavy shaper has DRIVE share above and CUT below median. Travel score is computed from the pre-move structural fingerprint using the LOO forecast pipeline of APPM-039.",
